{"id": "EUVD-2026-81997", "enisaUuid": "8d423d68-dd84-38bb-bc66-59461002d0ff", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nserial: core: clear freed pointers on uart_register_driver() failure\n\nuart_register_driver() leaves drv->state pointing to freed memory when\ntty_alloc_driver() fails. If tty_register_driver() fails, drv->tty_driver\nalso retains a pointer after its reference is dropped.\n\nDrivers that use drv->state as an \"already registered\" flag can then skip\nregistration on the next probe and pass the freed state to\nuart_add_one_port().\n\nThis issue was found with failslab on QEMU's raspi1ap board by\nfailing registration and binding the PL011 port again.\n\nClear both pointers on their failure paths, as uart_unregister_driver()\nalready does.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:08:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:05", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a9c0ffe5930c97b352f32febfc59a6e6ae6772ee", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/802e2192a9d38027730c2869c67c9131b8c8fe9f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ddf51d74ee9f9857c99477329d80408cedebda61", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/06b376432974fe5f25f2843a8e8438c6a1cf3d50", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/61a2fb25551be0375bc16ef2a70c987dfca26183"], "aliases": ["GHSA-wphw-rfmf-7hpg", "CVE-2026-90336"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "18aeb661-fee3-3a43-a7a3-b304997ee430", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "1d9fa457-e7e4-34ed-b373-4b81d1840874", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <802e2192a9d38027730c2869c67c9131b8c8fe9f"}, {"id": "1ef9582f-d62e-3798-8297-3712dd800186", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <a9c0ffe5930c97b352f32febfc59a6e6ae6772ee"}, {"id": "6617540c-